  "id": "COMPOUND:17776 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Lobelanidin appears to have a shared relationship with VMRC-MELG through a series of molecular targets, suggesting a potential pathway of interaction. The evidence indicates that Lobelanidin acts as a target for SF-188, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine. These compounds all ultimately target VMRC-MELG, indicating a possible cascade of molecular interactions. The presence of multiple targets and their shared final destination suggests that Lobelanidin may influence VMRC-MELG through a series of intermediate molecules, potentially modulating its activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Lobelanidin possibly acting as a bridge between its targets and VMRC-MELG. The evidence supports a mechanism where Lobelanidin indirectly affects VMRC-MELG via its targets, emphasizing the importance of these intermediaries in the overall biological process.",
